#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0308 expect=violation domain=LBX
#expectViolationCount 1
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when the DOMAIN value length is not equal to 2.
#note "The positive control for the `dataset_domain` migration (plans/PLAN-domain-expression-function.md): three rows, every one carrying a three-character DOMAIN, one finding. ⚑ What it actually pins is that the migrated Check still DETECTS a malformed domain — `dataset_domain` returns the row-0 DOMAIN cell VERBATIM, so `LBX` stays visible to a length check; the accessor does not normalise. ⚠⚠ It does NOT pin the dataset-constant fold, and the `#expectViolationCount 1` here must not be read as doing so: measured 2026-08-07, neutering `BroadcastFold.isDatasetFactCall` for `DS_DOMAIN` leaves this scenario GREEN at 1, because CDISC-CG0308 is `Sensitivity: Dataset` and RuleRunner collapses per-row bits to one violation whether or not the fact folds. The fold is pinned by `DatasetDomainFactTest` in corej-core, whose fixture rule is `Sensitivity: Record` so the collapse cannot mask it — there, the same neutering turns 1 into 2/3."
#library dataset-class LBX FINDINGS
dataset LBX label="Laboratory Test Results (malformed domain code)"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LBX | 01-701-1015 | ALB
CDISCPILOT01 | LBX | 01-701-1023 | ALT
CDISCPILOT01 | LBX | 01-701-1028 | AST
---
